      "be1520516017_html": "How Does It Work",
      "be939117180_html": "Products",
      "be121003098854_html": "Find Your Perfect&nbsp;<div>Solution and Sign Up</div>",
      "be912438447_html": "Take the quiz and select the product that’s right for you. Plans start at just £75, catering to every unique life situation. Most complete their plan in approximately 15 minutes, leaving tomorrow’s worries behind.",
      "be17636242956_html": "Making Estate Planning&nbsp;<div>Accessible to All</div>",
      "be553715299_html": "Estate planning is a significant matter, and we’ve made it accessible and affordable for all. Advisory Support is optional but recommended, especially for those seeking added peace of mind or personalised advice for more complex estates.",
      "be1847145170_html": "See all solutions",
      "be678265451_html": "Flexible Instalment Payment Option",
      "be630699727_html": "To make our services more accessible, we offer a flexible instalment payment option that allows you to manage costs over time while ensuring you receive the expert guidance and support you need.",
      "be283111775_html": "Login Now",
      "be719656772_html": "SOLUTION DRIVEN EXPERTISE",
      "be1561028954_html": "Tailored Plans for Every Life Situation",
      "be602328857856_html": "Effective estate planning is more important than ever. The <b>inheritance tax thresholds</b> (£325,000 nil-rate band and £175,000 residence nil-rate band) are frozen until 2030, potentially pushing more estates into the 40% tax bracket. From April 2026, <b>agricultural and business property relief</b> will provide 100% relief on the first £1 million, with 50% relief above this. Acting now can help protect assets and reduce tax exposure. <b>Capital gains tax </b>rates have increased to 18% (basic-rate taxpayers) and 24% (higher-rate taxpayers), with reduced exemptions requiring careful planning. From 2027, unspent <b>pension funds</b> will count towards estates for inheritance tax. <b>Stamp duty</b> relief ends in March 2025, raising costs for buyers. Employer <b>national insurance</b> contributions will rise from 2025, affecting business costs.",
      "be822706061131_html": "<i>“ Human nature stays the same, the one thing that stays constant, like death and taxes. And people still want good stories!”</i>",
      "be196046925520_html": "<i>– Alison Owen</i>",
      "be1371625978_html": "Nil Rate Band",
